sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Returning Customer
    participant WA as Meta Cloud API
    participant CE as Conversation Engine
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    Note over C,DB: FR-08 — BUILT (brief K, 10 October 2026). The suggestion is the customer's last order<br/>that the restaurant accepted, shown inside the first message at today's prices.<br/>NFR-03 (first message to confirmed order in under 30 seconds) is not measured yet.
    C->>WA: first message (no active session, or one that has just expired)
    WA->>CE: webhook — signature, dedup gate, restaurant open, orders not paused
    CE->>DB: any order of this customer not cancelled or expired, created in the last 3 hours?<br/>(idx_orders_customer_recent · the database's clock)
    alt yes — an order may still be on its way
        CE->>WA: welcome + menu, no suggestion
    else no
        CE->>DB: the last order with status accepted, preparing, ready or completed<br/>and its items (quantities summed per item, capped at 50)
        CE->>DB: today's catalog: names, prices, availability (item on and category on)
        alt no such order, or none of its items available today
            CE->>WA: welcome + menu, no suggestion
        else at least one item available
            CE->>CE: block: the available lines at today's prices and their total,<br/>a line naming the unavailable items, how to repeat the order
            alt welcome + block + menu over 4,096 characters
                CE->>WA: welcome + menu without the block (logged)
            else it fits
                CE->>DB: open the session as usual · context.reorder = order id + items
                CE->>WA: welcome + block + menu
            end
        end
    end
    C->>WA: the reorder word ("same")
    WA->>CE: webhook — the session is in browsing
    CE->>DB: SELECT the session FOR UPDATE
    alt no suggestion kept, or the cart is not empty
        CE->>WA: read as ordinary text, exactly as before FR-08
    else suggestion kept and the cart is empty
        CE->>DB: re-check every item live: available now, today's price
        alt none is still available
            CE->>WA: the missing items named + the empty-cart text · stays in browsing
        else at least one is still available
            CE->>DB: fill the cart · CAS browsing to fulfillment_choice<br/>(cart_review when pickup is the only option or already chosen)
            CE->>WA: missing items named first, then what the finish word sends:<br/>the pickup-or-delivery question, or the summary
            Note over C,DB: From here it is the ordinary path: pickup or delivery, the address,<br/>the summary and the confirm word. Building the cart is skipped.
        end
    end
